🔐 Caesar Cipher Web App – Encrypt & Decrypt Messages
📌 Project Overview
This project implements a Caesar Cipher encryption and decryption tool using Flask, a lightweight Python web framework. Users can enter a message, select encryption or decryption mode, and provide a shift value to encode or decode the text via a simple and interactive web interface.
🛠️ Technologies Used
Python 3

Flask

HTML + CSS (via templates/index.html)

💡 Features
Encrypt or decrypt any input text

User-friendly web interface

Handles both uppercase and lowercase letters

Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged

Session-based state retention

🧪 How It Works
The Caesar Cipher works by shifting each letter in the alphabet by a user-defined number:

Encryption shifts letters forward

Decryption shifts them backward

Wrap-around is handled using modulo arithmetic

Example:

Text: HELLO, Shift: 3, Encrypted: KHOOR

